{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "Reviewed join between the committed NumPy-oracle contracts and coverage catalog row ids, read by coverage/oracle_evidence.py. Every entry is validated on each run: target ids must exist in the catalog, explicit entries must be used, must not merely repeat what the automatic rules already resolve, and aliases must point at a row with direct contracts and must not shadow one. A corpus op key that neither the automatic rules nor this table resolve fails the generator.",
  "fuzz": {
    "bare_key_precedence": {
      "note": "A key without a dot names a top-level API. The FIRST existing callable/property row wins, so np.* shadows its np.linalg / np.random namesakes: the corpus keys trace/diagonal/outer/cross/vecdot/tensordot/matmul/matrix_transpose call np.<name> (gen_oracle.py) and power calls np.power; the np.linalg Array-API forms are credited only through the reviewed aliases below, never by name. Rows whose kind is class/constant/module are skipped here (np.fft is a module; fft resolves to np.fft.fft) and can only be targeted by an explicit key entry.",
      "templates": ["numpy.{key}", "numpy.linalg.{key}", "numpy.fft.{key}", "numpy.random.{key}", "numsharp.np.{key}"]
    },
    "prefix_rules": {
      "note": "A dotted key <head>.<rest> names a namespaced API. The first existing row among the head's templates wins; the numsharp.* fallback resolves NumSharp-only members the corpus gates (e.g. chebyshev.chebvalnd, NumSharp's N-D evaluation twin).",
      "ndarray": ["numpy.ndarray.{rest}", "numsharp.ndarray.{rest}"],
      "emath": ["numpy.emath.{rest}"],
      "ma": ["numpy.ma.{rest}", "numsharp.ma.{rest}"],
      "polynomial": ["numpy.polynomial.polynomial.{rest}", "numsharp.polynomial.polynomial.{rest}"],
